==Family background==
She is the daughter of [[John Connolly (hurler)|John Connolly]], who featured in Galway’s breakthrough [[All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship|All Ireland]] victory of [[All-Ireland Senior Hurling Championship 1980|1980]].{{fact|date=June 2020}}

==Career==
She exploded on to the sporting scene in Galway’s [[All-Ireland Minor Camogie Championship|All Ireland minor championship]] success of 2000. Having played as a sub in Galway’s narrowly unsuccessful team of 1999s she won player of the match as Galway beat Cork by 2-9 to 0-3 in Tullamore. She played on the [[University of Limerick]] team that won three [[Ashbourne Cup]] titles in a row in 2004,<ref>[http://www.RTÉ.ie/sport/2004/0215/camogie.html 2004 final UL 6-5 UCD 1-8, O'Toole Park, Crumlin, RTÉ online]</ref> 2005,<ref>[http://hoganstand.com/ArticleForm.aspx?ID=42733 2005 final UL 0-12 UCD 1-4 at Ballygunner, Hogan Stand]</ref> and 2006<ref>[http://www.sportfocus.com/newspub/story.cfm?ID= 17602 2006 final UL 0-13, UCD 1-9 at Limerick Gaelic Grounds, sportsfocus.com]{{dead link|date=June 2017 |bot=InternetArchiveBot |fix-attempted=yes }}</ref> She was nominated for an All Star award in 2009.<ref>She was the highest scoring forward of the competition during the [[National Camogie League|National League]] season of 2010.

==Other awards==
National League 2003 and 2005, [[All-Ireland Minor Camogie Championship|All Ireland Minor]] 2000, [[Ashbourne Cup]] winner with [[University of Limerick]] 2004, 2005 and 2006. 
